1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:04,199
(Previously) Currently, Her Highness is
suffering from renal failure.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,400
All the doctor can do is
manage her symptoms.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,200
I'm afraid that if I lose Grandmother,
I'll be left all alone.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,399
I have a request for you.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,000
Please don't be harsh on
Lord Vasin and Chatthorn.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,300
What did you do to my mother?!

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,499
You must choose now whether you will
side with your father or with him.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:40,000
Someone like him and someone like your
father can never live on the same land!

9
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:06,700
"The Edge of Horizon"
(Episode 11)

10
00:02:07,098 --> 00:02:09,099
[Nakhon Ratchasima]

11
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,803
Company, attention!

12
00:02:14,438 --> 00:02:16,022
Stand at ease!

13
00:02:18,782 --> 00:02:20,462
We'll serve as the main force,

14
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,664
leading three other forces
to surround the capital,

15
00:02:23,886 --> 00:02:25,987
to seize the self-serving government

16
00:02:26,366 --> 00:02:28,942
that is directing the economy
along communist lines.

17
00:02:29,529 --> 00:02:31,862
Those bastards will have
no place left in this country.

18
00:02:35,454 --> 00:02:37,662
We must reclaim our homeland,

19
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,580
no matter how much blood must be spilled.

20
00:02:40,121 --> 00:02:41,502
We must take it back at any cost.

21
00:02:42,038 --> 00:02:43,062
Will you stand and fight?

22
00:02:43,593 --> 00:02:46,628
We will fight! We will
fight! We will fight!

23
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,542
We will fight!

24
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:50,929
We will fight! We will
fight! We will fight!

25
00:03:08,302 --> 00:03:10,948
[Free Siam Movement Launched, Unveils Its
Principles to the Public for the First Time]

26
00:03:10,973 --> 00:03:13,423
I've sent forces to capture the
Free Siam members at Korat.

27
00:03:14,588 --> 00:03:16,222
They'll never make it to the capital.

28
00:03:30,534 --> 00:03:32,528
We decisively defeated

29
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,328
the government forces at Pak Chong.

30
00:03:46,923 --> 00:03:48,468
Read it, come on.

31
00:03:48,488 --> 00:03:50,368
FREE SIAM MOVEMENT DEALS GOVERNMENT POLICE

32
00:03:50,489 --> 00:03:54,328
A CRUSHING DEFEAT AT PAK CHONG

33
00:04:00,942 --> 00:04:03,462
[Khao Khu Ba Irrigation
Department, Saraburi]

34
00:04:43,142 --> 00:04:46,328
You Khana Ratsadon bastards are finished.

35
00:04:50,422 --> 00:04:52,423
[Lak Si Railway Station]

36
00:05:02,788 --> 00:05:04,481
We've secured this position, Your Highness.

37
00:05:04,505 --> 00:05:05,506
Great!

38
00:05:06,030 --> 00:05:07,922
I've spoken with the
commanders of each army.

39
00:05:08,513 --> 00:05:10,768
We can now make our intentions
known to the government.

40
00:05:13,968 --> 00:05:16,408
Attention! Eyes front! Present arms!

41
00:05:20,185 --> 00:05:22,265
The Free Siam Movement
has just issued an ultimatum,

42
00:05:22,564 --> 00:05:25,102
demanding that the
government resign within the hour.

43
00:05:25,604 --> 00:05:27,805
They will then take temporary
control of the country.

44
00:05:28,686 --> 00:05:30,076
What is the government going to do?

45
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:32,122
They've surrounded the capital.

46
00:05:32,196 --> 00:05:34,608
If word gets out, the people will panic.

47
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:54,888
At this moment, military and
civil officials throughout the Kingdom,

48
00:05:54,974 --> 00:05:57,448
having recognized the
threat posed to our nation

49
00:05:57,515 --> 00:05:59,448
and the Thai people

50
00:05:59,515 --> 00:06:02,048
by these enemies of the realm,

51
00:06:02,171 --> 00:06:05,288
shall unite to suppress them.

52
00:06:07,008 --> 00:06:08,168
The Free Siam Movement

53
00:06:08,459 --> 00:06:11,288
has mobilized forces
from Nakhon Ratchasima,

54
00:06:11,406 --> 00:06:14,568
Ubon Ratchathani, Saraburi, and Ayutthaya,

55
00:06:14,691 --> 00:06:16,502
and advanced upon the
outskirts of the capital.

56
00:06:16,526 --> 00:06:19,888
They have established
positions at Lak Si and Bang Khen,

57
00:06:20,190 --> 00:06:22,368
and issued an ultimatum demanding

58
00:06:22,568 --> 00:06:23,948
that the government surrender

59
00:06:24,328 --> 00:06:26,329
and restore power to His Majesty the King.

60
00:06:36,473 --> 00:06:38,502
Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin!

61
00:06:38,638 --> 00:06:40,822
Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin!

62
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:43,502
- Mr. Tin!
- What is going on?

63
00:06:45,332 --> 00:06:46,935
Are we really going to war?

64
00:06:48,681 --> 00:06:50,502
If they really make it into the capital,

65
00:06:50,968 --> 00:06:51,969
I won't let them.

66
00:06:53,449 --> 00:06:56,012
My father said we must stand together
to protect the capital.

67
00:06:56,723 --> 00:06:58,683
What are we going to
do if war really breaks out?

68
00:06:59,123 --> 00:07:03,152
- What should we do?
- Everyone, calm down.

69
00:07:03,470 --> 00:07:04,471
You need to focus.

70
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:06,590
You need to calm down, nothing is happening.

71
00:07:06,742 --> 00:07:08,702
For now, wait for further news.

72
00:07:09,316 --> 00:07:12,622
Everyone, go home. Take care of yourselves

73
00:07:12,961 --> 00:07:14,742
and your families. Understood?

74
00:07:15,342 --> 00:07:17,062
- Got it, sir.
- Come on, let's go.

75
00:07:18,542 --> 00:07:19,702
Take care, kids.

76
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:21,422
You too.

77
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:24,582
I think things are getting out of hand.

78
00:07:25,545 --> 00:07:27,262
The people are split into two factions.

79
00:07:27,844 --> 00:07:29,702
One supports the Free Siam Movement,

80
00:07:30,076 --> 00:07:32,174
saying it will save the country
and make things better.

81
00:07:32,198 --> 00:07:35,038
The other disagrees, saying the government
has accomplished quite a lot.

82
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:39,068
I'm sure a major confrontation
will break out before long.

83
00:07:41,702 --> 00:07:45,303
I can only hope nothing terrible happens.

84
00:07:46,961 --> 00:07:49,233
I hope everyone makes it home safely

85
00:07:49,532 --> 00:07:51,022
to the people they love.

86
00:08:01,202 --> 00:08:05,572
Grandma, please watch over us all
from above and keep everyone safe.

87
00:08:06,562 --> 00:08:08,372
Please don't let anything happen to anyone.

88
00:08:23,388 --> 00:08:26,532
The government now holds the upper hand.

89
00:08:26,786 --> 00:08:30,052
The provincial troops supporting
the Free Siam Movement are faltering.

90
00:08:30,402 --> 00:08:33,186
Should they refuse to surrender,

91
00:08:33,383 --> 00:08:34,703
they will be dealt with severely.

92
00:08:35,826 --> 00:08:36,852
Your Highness,

93
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:40,192
could the fighting reach our home?

94
00:08:40,661 --> 00:08:42,812
We're so close to Bang Khen.

95
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:49,432
We need to run, come on!

96
00:09:19,394 --> 00:09:20,572
Your Highness, watch out!

97
00:09:26,268 --> 00:09:27,269
Your Highness!

98
00:09:55,247 --> 00:09:56,248
Let's go!

99
00:11:02,652 --> 00:11:03,653
Your Highness!

100
00:11:07,272 --> 00:11:08,273
Your Highness!

101
00:11:13,573 --> 00:11:14,574
Your Highness.

102
00:11:14,751 --> 00:11:15,752
Phob?

103
00:11:24,252 --> 00:11:25,253
Let's go.

104
00:11:51,772 --> 00:11:52,773
Please have a seat here.

105
00:11:56,527 --> 00:11:57,528
Easy there.

106
00:12:08,548 --> 00:12:09,868
Stay here tonight, Your Highness.

107
00:12:11,042 --> 00:12:12,826
We're quite far from the front lines,

108
00:12:13,503 --> 00:12:14,504
so it should be safe.

109
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:18,092
I'm worried about Aum.

110
00:12:39,286 --> 00:12:40,287
Tomorrow.

111
00:12:41,398 --> 00:12:43,278
I will look for her first
thing in the morning.

112
00:12:44,272 --> 00:12:45,530
Don't worry, Your Highness.

113
00:12:50,627 --> 00:12:51,628
Thank you.

114
00:13:03,630 --> 00:13:04,631
Ow!

115
00:13:04,888 --> 00:13:05,889
Your Highness!

116
00:13:10,168 --> 00:13:11,169
Please have a seat here.

117
00:13:20,502 --> 00:13:21,503
Did your ankle hurt?

118
00:13:22,438 --> 00:13:23,448
I think so.

119
00:13:27,312 --> 00:13:28,328
Hey, Phob. It's fine.

120
00:13:29,590 --> 00:13:30,591
You don't have to.

121
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:32,288
Let me look at it.

122
00:14:00,931 --> 00:14:01,932
This might hurt a little.

123
00:14:49,216 --> 00:14:50,328
Thank you.

124
00:14:55,888 --> 00:14:58,768
Thank you for risking your life to save me.

125
00:15:04,864 --> 00:15:06,648
You know I was willing to risk it,

126
00:15:12,632 --> 00:15:13,633
even if it meant that

127
00:15:16,451 --> 00:15:17,452
everything had changed.

128
00:15:23,115 --> 00:15:24,248
Even if both of us

129
00:15:26,944 --> 00:15:28,648
could never be the way we were before,

130
00:15:51,806 --> 00:15:53,608
I would still want to care for you

131
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,768
and protect you,

132
00:16:12,222 --> 00:16:13,782
no matter what role I had in your life.

133
00:16:19,865 --> 00:16:23,688
Whether you forgive me or not,

134
00:16:28,888 --> 00:16:30,648
I will forever

135
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:34,848
be your Phob.

136
00:17:01,638 --> 00:17:03,808
We've secured Bang Khen as our stronghold.

137
00:17:04,728 --> 00:17:06,488
If we can hold this line,

138
00:17:06,779 --> 00:17:08,688
we'll advance into the capital together

139
00:17:09,787 --> 00:17:11,627
once reinforcements
from the provinces arrive.

140
00:17:12,832 --> 00:17:14,862
The news from the capital
is not good, Your Highness.

141
00:17:14,886 --> 00:17:17,086
Many people have come out
in support of the government.

142
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:21,008
Our troops are growing weary,
and several units have suffered casualties.

143
00:17:22,158 --> 00:17:25,248
Some are beginning to wonder
whether we can really win.

144
00:17:28,568 --> 00:17:29,569
Listen carefully.

145
00:17:31,064 --> 00:17:33,448
We've come too far to turn back now.

146
00:17:34,928 --> 00:17:42,019
What we have to do now is hold the front line
and wait for reinforcements from the provinces.

147
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,448
Victory must be ours...

148
00:17:45,054 --> 00:17:47,128
not for our own sake,

149
00:17:47,848 --> 00:17:48,968
but for Siam.

150
00:18:16,144 --> 00:18:17,145
Aum!

151
00:18:18,167 --> 00:18:19,968
- Aum!
- Prince Tinnakorn!

152
00:18:25,987 --> 00:18:28,088
- Oh, Your Highness.
- It's okay.

153
00:18:32,182 --> 00:18:33,248
How are you?

154
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:36,648
I'm okay. How are you? Did you get hurt?

155
00:18:37,448 --> 00:18:38,449
I'm fine.

156
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,204
Aum,

157
00:18:43,406 --> 00:18:44,407
I think…

158
00:18:45,352 --> 00:18:47,448
you should freshen up and get some rest.

159
00:18:48,206 --> 00:18:49,207
Yeah, I think I should.

160
00:18:59,091 --> 00:19:00,092
Phob, thank you.

161
00:19:09,307 --> 00:19:10,308
Is everything okay?

162
00:19:13,451 --> 00:19:14,928
I have received orders

163
00:19:17,547 --> 00:19:19,328
to lead the troops to Bang Khen tomorrow.

164
00:19:22,704 --> 00:19:25,128
Prince Vasin and Prince
Chatthorn are there.

165
00:19:26,808 --> 00:19:28,288
How is the situation now, Phob?

166
00:19:29,635 --> 00:19:31,155
We still don't know how this will end,

167
00:19:32,888 --> 00:19:34,328
but I've received reports that

168
00:19:35,568 --> 00:19:37,408
the Free Siam side is running into trouble.

169
00:19:39,683 --> 00:19:41,083
Several members of the royal family

170
00:19:41,383 --> 00:19:44,008
have no experience
leading troops in the field,

171
00:19:45,315 --> 00:19:46,888
which has led to repeated mistakes.

172
00:19:48,808 --> 00:19:50,128
What about my dad and my brother?

173
00:19:54,904 --> 00:19:56,128
Don't your worry.

174
00:19:56,536 --> 00:19:58,288
I promised your grandma

175
00:20:00,979 --> 00:20:03,248
that I would never hurt Prince Vasin

176
00:20:03,539 --> 00:20:04,540
and Prince Chatthorn.

177
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,728
- Even if it costs me my life...
- Don't say that.

178
00:20:14,608 --> 00:20:16,208
Can you please stop talking about death?

179
00:20:17,307 --> 00:20:18,308
Please?

180
00:20:22,368 --> 00:20:24,369
I've already lost my grandma.

181
00:20:27,963 --> 00:20:29,568
I don't want to lose anyone else.

182
00:21:13,368 --> 00:21:14,369
Phob.

183
00:21:17,608 --> 00:21:19,209
Promise me one thing.

184
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:28,808
Promise me that you will come back.

185
00:21:42,614 --> 00:21:43,648
I promise.

186
00:21:46,214 --> 00:21:47,315
I promise

187
00:21:49,088 --> 00:21:50,368
that I will come back to you.

188
00:21:52,888 --> 00:21:54,008
Promise me.

189
00:23:38,411 --> 00:23:40,168
Get the villagers out of here! Come on!

190
00:23:53,803 --> 00:23:55,328
Hurry! Let's go.

191
00:23:56,208 --> 00:23:57,608
Hurry! Hurry!

192
00:23:58,824 --> 00:23:59,825
Mom!

193
00:24:02,928 --> 00:24:04,208
Mom! I'm scared!

194
00:24:10,915 --> 00:24:11,916
Let's get out of here.

195
00:24:27,014 --> 00:24:28,869
Drop your pistol!

196
00:24:29,043 --> 00:24:30,044
Come on!

197
00:25:08,179 --> 00:25:09,448
I've been waiting for you,

198
00:25:10,068 --> 00:25:11,248
you miserable servant!

199
00:25:38,027 --> 00:25:40,528
You see now?

200
00:25:42,048 --> 00:25:45,549
Someone like you can
only ever be a lowly servant.

201
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:48,600
You're nothing but dust beneath my feet.
That's all you'll ever be.

202
00:25:48,832 --> 00:25:50,133
Can you see it now?

203
00:25:56,568 --> 00:25:57,569
That's enough.

204
00:25:59,288 --> 00:26:01,008
Dad, why don't we just kill him?

205
00:26:01,358 --> 00:26:04,368
A traitor like this deserves to die.
Why are we keeping him alive?

206
00:26:05,408 --> 00:26:06,448
He's still useful.

207
00:26:07,160 --> 00:26:09,640
We can use him as leverage in negotiations
with the government.

208
00:26:13,022 --> 00:26:14,208
Do you really think

209
00:26:16,019 --> 00:26:18,139
you're still in a position
to bargain, Your Highness?

210
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,968
I've seen your military camp.

211
00:26:25,342 --> 00:26:26,702
It's overflowing with the wounded,

212
00:26:27,868 --> 00:26:29,088
supplies are running low,

213
00:26:31,308 --> 00:26:32,568
and morale is plummeting.

214
00:26:35,046 --> 00:26:37,688
It won't be long before
your forces are overrun.

215
00:26:38,278 --> 00:26:40,208
Provincial reinforcements are coming.

216
00:26:41,208 --> 00:26:43,609
Once they arrive, victory will be ours.

217
00:26:44,209 --> 00:26:47,128
I won't let you and your people cause
any more trouble in this country.

218
00:26:47,171 --> 00:26:48,888
And who is causing the chaos now?

219
00:26:51,752 --> 00:26:53,588
When we brought change to this country,

220
00:26:54,659 --> 00:26:56,608
not a single drop of blood was shed.

221
00:26:58,078 --> 00:26:59,468
But look at what you've done.

222
00:27:00,408 --> 00:27:01,985
How many more people
are you going to let die?

223
00:27:02,009 --> 00:27:04,048
Because you used dirty tactics.

224
00:27:04,408 --> 00:27:06,608
You deceived everyone with your schemes,

225
00:27:07,144 --> 00:27:08,728
just like you deceived my son.

226
00:27:09,811 --> 00:27:11,328
I've never lied to him.

227
00:27:12,819 --> 00:27:14,168
I love Prince Tinnakorn.

228
00:27:22,344 --> 00:27:23,345
What did you say?

229
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:27,560
What are you talking about?

230
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:32,608
I asked you, what did you just say?

231
00:27:33,001 --> 00:27:34,002
What did you say?

232
00:27:38,528 --> 00:27:39,968
Prince Tinnakorn and I…

233
00:27:42,171 --> 00:27:44,808
- we are...
- It's not true. I don't believe you.

234
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:46,921
No… no.

235
00:27:47,968 --> 00:27:50,488
No… no, this isn't real.

236
00:27:51,774 --> 00:27:52,775
It can't be.

237
00:27:52,937 --> 00:27:53,938
I don't believe you.

238
00:27:54,488 --> 00:27:56,048
Dad? It's not true, isn't it?

239
00:27:57,771 --> 00:27:59,288
My brother wouldn't…

240
00:27:59,488 --> 00:28:01,848
No way, he wouldn't do
it with a servant like you.

241
00:28:01,915 --> 00:28:04,268
With a servant like you? No way!

242
00:28:05,088 --> 00:28:07,088
Dad! No way!

243
00:28:09,768 --> 00:28:10,769
Ugh!

244
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:15,831
Chat!

245
00:28:18,064 --> 00:28:19,065
Stop!

246
00:28:24,027 --> 00:28:25,288
We need him alive.

247
00:28:31,747 --> 00:28:33,648
Just wait until we win.

248
00:28:35,128 --> 00:28:37,008
And I will kill him myself.

249
00:29:01,496 --> 00:29:03,688
Your Highness.

250
00:29:05,368 --> 00:29:07,214
I heard that…

251
00:29:07,607 --> 00:29:10,034
There's heavy gunfire at Bang Khen Market.

252
00:29:11,168 --> 00:29:15,048
Your father's forces have captured
many government soldiers.

253
00:29:15,624 --> 00:29:16,625
Bang Khen Market?

254
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:19,848
I have received orders

255
00:29:20,568 --> 00:29:22,328
to lead the troops to Bang Khen tomorrow.

256
00:29:23,984 --> 00:29:26,418
Prince Vasin and Prince
Chatthorn are there.

257
00:29:27,344 --> 00:29:28,345
Phob.

258
00:29:33,168 --> 00:29:34,169
[Lak Si Railway Station]

259
00:29:35,046 --> 00:29:37,408
We have wounded men!
Get beds for the soldiers, quickly!

260
00:29:38,923 --> 00:29:40,248
There are wounded soldiers!

261
00:29:45,216 --> 00:29:47,288
You can't go in. Please leave this area.

262
00:29:48,155 --> 00:29:49,418
I'm here to see Prince Vasin.

263
00:29:51,088 --> 00:29:52,888
I am Tinnakorn Varakulvatin, I'm his son.

264
00:29:53,568 --> 00:29:54,569
Tin.

265
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:56,292
Chat?

266
00:29:59,211 --> 00:30:01,212
Did you take Phob into custody?

267
00:30:03,366 --> 00:30:04,367
Phob is here, isn't he?

268
00:30:26,468 --> 00:30:28,628
Did the government refuse
to negotiate, Your Highness?

269
00:30:33,068 --> 00:30:34,868
Or have the troops
from the east not arrived?

270
00:30:36,803 --> 00:30:38,368
Don't get smart with me, Phob.

271
00:30:40,643 --> 00:30:41,644
Your Highness,

272
00:30:43,435 --> 00:30:44,755
please order the remaining troops

273
00:30:46,576 --> 00:30:47,818
to withdraw.

274
00:30:51,488 --> 00:30:53,048
Don't let any more lives be lost.

275
00:30:55,590 --> 00:30:56,591
As someone

276
00:30:59,110 --> 00:31:00,768
who deeply respect you,

277
00:31:02,711 --> 00:31:03,728
Your Highness, please.

278
00:31:06,584 --> 00:31:07,688
I'm begging you to retreat.

279
00:31:09,726 --> 00:31:11,888
I don't want anything to happen to you.

280
00:31:15,352 --> 00:31:16,353
Retreat?

281
00:31:18,387 --> 00:31:21,248
We've come too far for
that. There's no turning back.

282
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:23,728
We must fight to the very end.

283
00:31:30,288 --> 00:31:31,289
Phob?

284
00:31:31,298 --> 00:31:33,408
Tin, how did you get here?

285
00:31:34,774 --> 00:31:35,775
Your Highness.

286
00:31:35,795 --> 00:31:36,995
What happened to you?

287
00:31:40,968 --> 00:31:42,528
Dad, what did you do to him?

288
00:31:45,248 --> 00:31:46,249
Are you okay?

289
00:31:48,184 --> 00:31:49,728
Phob? Chat.

290
00:31:50,430 --> 00:31:52,910
I'm asking you. Please don't hurt him.

291
00:31:53,648 --> 00:31:56,768
I brought you here to watch him die.

292
00:31:57,174 --> 00:32:00,088
You'll see it with your own eyes,
and maybe you'll stop being so stupid.

293
00:32:00,267 --> 00:32:02,128
Please, Chat. Don't do anything to Phob.

294
00:32:02,411 --> 00:32:03,412
Please.

295
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:08,160
- What are you doing? Get up!
- Please don't hurt him.

296
00:32:08,312 --> 00:32:10,113
Tin, get up!

297
00:32:10,248 --> 00:32:11,488
- Chat.
- Get up!

298
00:32:12,849 --> 00:32:14,488
Have you ever thought that

299
00:32:15,550 --> 00:32:19,008
things wouldn't have turned out this way
if he hadn't come back?

300
00:32:22,728 --> 00:32:24,488
Grandma would still be alive,

301
00:32:24,875 --> 00:32:26,268
our palace would still be ours,

302
00:32:27,868 --> 00:32:29,968
and our family wouldn't
have fallen apart like this.

303
00:32:32,598 --> 00:32:33,888
Stop blaming everyone else.

304
00:32:35,608 --> 00:32:38,448
You're the one who ruined
everything, Prince Chat.

305
00:32:38,888 --> 00:32:41,664
You embezzled public funds, and
you were forced to sell your own palace.

306
00:32:41,688 --> 00:32:42,689
Shut up.

307
00:32:43,126 --> 00:32:44,127
You need to shut up!

308
00:32:44,808 --> 00:32:47,888
You're the one who made everything
turn out this way. It's all because of you!

309
00:32:48,635 --> 00:32:49,636
Chat.

310
00:32:52,022 --> 00:32:54,823
Can you take all your
personal anger out on me?

311
00:32:56,318 --> 00:32:57,568
The country's transformation

312
00:32:58,360 --> 00:33:00,488
would have happened with or without Phob.

313
00:33:02,504 --> 00:33:05,888
But I'm the one who disgraced
the Varakulvatin family.

314
00:33:06,955 --> 00:33:08,008
It's me.

315
00:33:08,774 --> 00:33:11,808
If you need someone to hate,

316
00:33:12,736 --> 00:33:13,737
it should be me.

317
00:33:15,222 --> 00:33:16,848
Tin, what are you doing?

318
00:33:17,392 --> 00:33:18,968
I'm the one who started all of this.

319
00:33:19,568 --> 00:33:21,469
If you have to kill someone, kill me.

320
00:33:21,531 --> 00:33:22,608
What are you doing?

321
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:26,088
What is it? Are you willing to die for him?

322
00:33:27,774 --> 00:33:29,014
If the situation were reversed,

323
00:33:29,811 --> 00:33:33,368
and Phob were about
to do this to you and Dad,

324
00:33:34,328 --> 00:33:35,947
I'd do exactly the same.

325
00:33:35,974 --> 00:33:39,208
Everyone here is someone I love.

326
00:33:42,248 --> 00:33:45,368
Please… why can't we just talk this out,
just this once?

327
00:33:45,378 --> 00:33:46,379
Tin.

328
00:33:46,559 --> 00:33:48,958
- Why does it always have to end up like this?
- Tin!

329
00:33:53,544 --> 00:33:55,808
If you need to kill someone, kill me.

330
00:34:01,507 --> 00:34:02,508
Do you know?

331
00:34:07,358 --> 00:34:08,688
All my life,

332
00:34:11,014 --> 00:34:14,048
I've tried to catch up with you,

333
00:34:18,611 --> 00:34:21,308
but no matter how hard I
tried, I could never keep up.

334
00:34:28,048 --> 00:34:30,568
You were Dad's pride.

335
00:34:34,734 --> 00:34:37,518
You brought honor to our royal family.

336
00:34:41,016 --> 00:34:42,408
You were everything.

337
00:34:43,688 --> 00:34:45,153
I wanted to be.

338
00:34:54,816 --> 00:34:55,817
Chat!

339
00:34:56,662 --> 00:34:58,063
Don't hurt your brother.

340
00:34:59,728 --> 00:35:01,088
He's your brother, don't hurt him.

341
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:07,888
I was jealous of you.

342
00:35:09,128 --> 00:35:10,808
I've always been jealous of you.

343
00:35:12,349 --> 00:35:14,968
Tin, I'm jealous of you.

344
00:35:23,248 --> 00:35:25,368
But you're my little brother.

345
00:35:30,406 --> 00:35:32,328
I could never hate you,

346
00:35:39,099 --> 00:35:40,868
and I never wanted to hurt you.

347
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:13,920
The defenses have been breached.
Please leave at once, Your Highness.

348
00:36:16,931 --> 00:36:17,932
Dad!

349
00:36:18,083 --> 00:36:19,728
- Tin, let's go!
- Your Highness!

350
00:36:20,168 --> 00:36:21,169
Your Highness!

351
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:22,968
- You have to run!
- Your Highness!

352
00:36:23,384 --> 00:36:24,385
Your Highness!

353
00:36:25,576 --> 00:36:26,577
Your Highness!

354
00:36:56,635 --> 00:36:57,636
Tin!

355
00:36:58,656 --> 00:36:59,657
- Let's go!
- Tin!

356
00:37:06,068 --> 00:37:07,069
Tin!

357
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:14,961
Phob!

358
00:37:27,018 --> 00:37:28,019
Tin!

359
00:37:28,211 --> 00:37:29,212
Watch out!

360
00:37:45,771 --> 00:37:46,772
Your Highness!

361
00:38:16,088 --> 00:38:17,089
Phob?

362
00:38:19,371 --> 00:38:20,372
Phob!

363
00:38:26,464 --> 00:38:27,465
Phob?

364
00:38:27,856 --> 00:38:28,857
Phob.

365
00:38:36,464 --> 00:38:37,465
Phob.

366
00:38:43,039 --> 00:38:44,168
- Phob.
- Your Highness.

367
00:38:44,422 --> 00:38:45,423
Phob.

368
00:38:49,312 --> 00:38:50,313
Phob.

369
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:51,881
Phob.

370
00:38:53,219 --> 00:38:54,368
Phob, are you okay?

371
00:38:57,438 --> 00:38:59,328
Are you alright? Are you hurt?

372
00:38:59,363 --> 00:39:00,364
I'm okay.

373
00:39:00,771 --> 00:39:01,968
Phob, please be okay.

374
00:39:02,572 --> 00:39:03,968
Don't cry, Your Highness.

375
00:39:05,312 --> 00:39:06,968
Your Phob is here with you.

376
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:10,528
Phob, I'll get you out of here.

377
00:39:10,904 --> 00:39:12,488
I'll take you to the hospital.

378
00:39:12,979 --> 00:39:14,328
Phob, let's go.

379
00:39:16,264 --> 00:39:17,265
Is it hurt?

380
00:39:32,363 --> 00:39:33,364
Your Highness.

381
00:39:34,928 --> 00:39:36,728
Can you forgive me?

382
00:39:39,329 --> 00:39:40,848
I told you, I'm not angry.

383
00:39:41,328 --> 00:39:42,968
I understand everything you've done.

384
00:39:45,499 --> 00:39:46,618
I didn't do this

385
00:39:49,894 --> 00:39:51,688
solely for the sake of the country.

386
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:54,368
Deep down,

387
00:39:56,795 --> 00:39:58,248
I hoped that

388
00:40:00,454 --> 00:40:01,968
if the world changed,

389
00:40:03,702 --> 00:40:05,448
and the class divide

390
00:40:06,352 --> 00:40:07,353
grew narrower,

391
00:40:09,472 --> 00:40:10,728
things between us

392
00:40:12,582 --> 00:40:13,928
might become easier.

393
00:40:17,005 --> 00:40:18,006
We…

394
00:40:20,120 --> 00:40:22,568
we wouldn't have to hide our love,

395
00:40:25,534 --> 00:40:27,128
and we wouldn't have to be torn apart.

396
00:40:28,099 --> 00:40:31,032
I know. I understand it all.

397
00:40:32,008 --> 00:40:33,523
And I'm right here with you.

398
00:40:35,832 --> 00:40:38,048
I'm here with you, please
don't ever leave me.

399
00:40:40,883 --> 00:40:42,208
I love you, Your Highness.

400
00:40:44,184 --> 00:40:45,185
No matter what.

401
00:40:46,808 --> 00:40:49,928
I will be your Phob

402
00:40:50,830 --> 00:40:51,831
forever.

403
00:40:53,518 --> 00:40:54,519
No!

404
00:40:55,288 --> 00:40:57,168
I'm right here, please don't leave me.

405
00:40:58,072 --> 00:40:59,073
Phob.

406
00:41:02,942 --> 00:41:03,943
Tin.

407
00:41:04,120 --> 00:41:05,121
Tin.

408
00:41:06,862 --> 00:41:08,488
We have to go.

409
00:41:09,011 --> 00:41:09,848
Let's go!

410
00:41:09,878 --> 00:41:11,328
- Dad! Help him!
- Your Highness!

411
00:41:11,598 --> 00:41:13,168
- Let's go!
- Your Highness!

412
00:41:13,405 --> 00:41:14,608
- Let's go!
- Your Highness!

413
00:41:16,368 --> 00:41:18,728
- You have to run!
- Your Highness!

414
00:42:00,643 --> 00:42:02,088
- Phob!
- Tin! Let's go!

415
00:42:07,083 --> 00:42:08,084
Phob.

416
00:42:09,227 --> 00:42:10,328
- Phob!
- Come on!

417
00:42:10,408 --> 00:42:11,409
Your Highness!

418
00:42:14,326 --> 00:42:15,368
- Phob!
- Come with me!

419
00:42:17,068 --> 00:42:18,069
Your Highness!

420
00:42:21,768 --> 00:42:22,769
Your Highness!

421
00:43:00,104 --> 00:43:01,688
I'm not dreaming, am I?

422
00:43:03,654 --> 00:43:04,655
You're dreaming, Phob.

423
00:43:07,768 --> 00:43:08,928
You'll wake up soon.

424
00:43:15,147 --> 00:43:16,288
If this is a dream,

425
00:43:17,608 --> 00:43:19,448
then let me remain in it forever.

426
00:43:22,128 --> 00:43:23,368
I never wish to wake.

427
00:43:24,528 --> 00:43:26,768
Then I hope you never wake up.

428
00:44:33,229 --> 00:44:36,448
Right now the unrest

429
00:44:36,699 --> 00:44:37,988
has come to an end.

430
00:44:38,566 --> 00:44:42,088
Government forces have
regained control of the situation

431
00:44:42,307 --> 00:44:45,268
and restored peace to the nation.

432
00:44:46,168 --> 00:44:48,328
Those involved in the insurrection

433
00:44:48,504 --> 00:44:51,048
will be investigated

434
00:44:51,105 --> 00:44:55,528
and brought before the courts
in accordance with the law.

435
00:45:18,388 --> 00:45:19,448
You can't sleep?

436
00:45:23,568 --> 00:45:24,569
No, I can't.

437
00:45:39,568 --> 00:45:40,569
Chat,

438
00:45:46,918 --> 00:45:47,968
I am sorry.

439
00:45:57,718 --> 00:45:59,268
Why are you apologizing to me?

440
00:46:04,728 --> 00:46:06,368
For bringing you to this point

441
00:46:07,757 --> 00:46:09,168
and making you end up in prison.

442
00:46:12,078 --> 00:46:13,768
I've never blamed you.

443
00:46:15,411 --> 00:46:17,208
Dad, I made my own decision.

444
00:46:18,568 --> 00:46:20,809
I chose this path myself.

445
00:46:24,336 --> 00:46:26,968
I was the one who led
you down this path, too.

446
00:46:31,088 --> 00:46:33,576
- I failed as a dad...
- No, you're not.

447
00:46:42,110 --> 00:46:43,268
There's something else.

448
00:46:44,111 --> 00:46:46,168
I've wanted to apologize to you for.

449
00:46:55,088 --> 00:46:57,048
I was never fair to you.

450
00:47:00,571 --> 00:47:01,572
Dad?

451
00:47:05,963 --> 00:47:08,168
I kept comparing you to Tinnakorn.

452
00:47:10,422 --> 00:47:12,238
I was always praising Tinnakorn

453
00:47:13,968 --> 00:47:16,328
and expecting you to be like him,

454
00:47:20,088 --> 00:47:23,008
until I forgot that you
were your own person.

455
00:47:26,072 --> 00:47:29,288
It was because I was no good.

456
00:47:30,232 --> 00:47:32,833
I was a disappointment.
I was the one who embarrassed you.

457
00:47:34,670 --> 00:47:36,771
But I'm the one who made you believe

458
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:39,268
you were never good enough.

459
00:48:01,197 --> 00:48:02,198
Sometimes,

460
00:48:06,563 --> 00:48:07,648
I just want to hear you say

461
00:48:12,120 --> 00:48:14,939
you're proud of me.

462
00:48:36,595 --> 00:48:37,848
I'm sorry, son.

463
00:49:06,696 --> 00:49:07,697
Get some sleep.

464
00:49:10,768 --> 00:49:11,769
Come here.

465
00:50:33,160 --> 00:50:34,928
Tin, how are you doing?

466
00:50:36,787 --> 00:50:37,947
I'm doing so much better now.

467
00:50:38,648 --> 00:50:40,649
The doctor should let me go home soon.

468
00:50:43,726 --> 00:50:45,168
You need to get better soon.

469
00:50:46,280 --> 00:50:48,268
Then we can go visit Uncle and Chat.

470
00:50:51,102 --> 00:50:52,103
Siri,

471
00:50:53,355 --> 00:50:54,888
Have you heard any news about Phob?

472
00:50:57,222 --> 00:51:00,008
Janthorn is searching for him.

473
00:51:00,496 --> 00:51:03,590
Maybe he was injured

474
00:51:04,168 --> 00:51:06,088
and taken somewhere else for treatment.

475
00:51:24,395 --> 00:51:25,568
Have you found Phob?

476
00:51:40,139 --> 00:51:41,808
You found Phob, didn't you, Janthorn?

477
00:51:50,808 --> 00:51:52,409
He's safe, right?

478
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:06,688
You found him, didn't you?

479
00:53:22,486 --> 00:53:23,487
Nual said

480
00:53:24,672 --> 00:53:25,688
they found the rings

481
00:53:27,542 --> 00:53:29,328
on the ground near Phob's body.

482
00:53:32,994 --> 00:53:35,656
So she gave them to me.

483
00:53:37,608 --> 00:53:39,808
She thought I might want them.

484
00:53:53,238 --> 00:53:54,239
Do you know

485
00:53:55,688 --> 00:53:57,728
that he promised he would come back?

486
00:54:05,435 --> 00:54:07,168
He has never broken his promises,

487
00:54:08,390 --> 00:54:09,391
not once.

488
00:54:21,232 --> 00:54:22,233
Phob,

489
00:54:24,806 --> 00:54:25,807
where are you?

490
00:54:28,752 --> 00:54:30,168
Come back now.

491
00:54:30,965 --> 00:54:31,966
Tin.

492
00:54:40,686 --> 00:54:43,048
You promised you'd come back to me.

493
00:54:46,379 --> 00:54:47,648
Please come back to me now.

494
00:56:30,675 --> 00:56:31,676
Phob,

495
00:56:34,531 --> 00:56:35,808
I am sorry.

496
00:56:39,508 --> 00:56:44,648
I'm sorry I stood between you
and the happiness you wanted.

497
00:57:20,180 --> 00:57:21,528
Dad? Chat?

498
00:57:26,211 --> 00:57:27,212
Tin.

499
00:57:29,088 --> 00:57:30,368
How are you?

500
00:58:43,248 --> 00:58:45,249
[One month later]

501
00:58:49,259 --> 00:58:51,899
I have an interview with them
about the restoration of this palace,

502
00:58:51,984 --> 00:58:55,008
so I thought you might like to come along.

503
00:59:01,918 --> 00:59:03,328
It's heartbreaking.

504
00:59:04,819 --> 00:59:06,467
The Varakulvatin Palace

505
00:59:07,758 --> 00:59:09,268
has now become a hotel.

506
00:59:15,326 --> 00:59:17,926
It's still a good thing that they
at least preserved the building.

507
00:59:19,966 --> 00:59:23,208
Janthorn, thank you so
much for inviting me here.

508
01:00:32,731 --> 01:00:36,368
I hereby appoint you as my knight.

509
01:00:37,691 --> 01:00:38,692
Thank you, Your Highness.

510
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:55,768
I don't have a garland, so this
cotton rose will have to do for now.

511
01:00:57,168 --> 01:00:58,568
Does that mean

512
01:00:59,771 --> 01:01:02,972
you've chosen me, Your Highness?

513
01:01:30,648 --> 01:01:33,208
After all I've done,
do you still think I despise you, Phob?

514
01:01:56,776 --> 01:01:58,968
Whether it takes months, years,

515
01:01:59,368 --> 01:02:00,369
or a lifetime,

516
01:02:01,267 --> 01:02:03,488
I will wait for you and you alone.

517
01:02:05,459 --> 01:02:07,488
I will always be your Phob

518
01:02:08,344 --> 01:02:10,768
no matter what.

519
01:02:28,182 --> 01:02:29,368
Where are you?

520
01:02:30,830 --> 01:02:32,268
Where are you, Your Highness?

521
01:02:32,862 --> 01:02:33,863
Are you here?

522
01:02:35,032 --> 01:02:37,928
Oh my, where are you?

523
01:02:39,418 --> 01:02:40,498
There you are, I found you!

524
01:02:42,054 --> 01:02:44,218
You found me again.

525
01:02:45,131 --> 01:02:48,688
No matter where you are, I will find you.

526
01:03:54,395 --> 01:03:55,448
Phob, is that you?

527
01:04:12,448 --> 01:04:13,808
Am I dreaming?

528
01:04:49,451 --> 01:04:50,452
Phob?

529
01:04:50,656 --> 01:04:52,528
Do you still think you're dreaming?

530
01:04:53,200 --> 01:04:54,201
Phob.

531
01:04:57,808 --> 01:04:58,809
Phob.

532
01:05:03,248 --> 01:05:04,288
It really is you.

533
01:05:12,472 --> 01:05:14,408
I thought I'd never
see you again in this life.

534
01:05:16,040 --> 01:05:17,488
What did I promise you?

535
01:05:19,118 --> 01:05:20,128
That no matter what,

536
01:05:21,656 --> 01:05:23,088
I would always come back to you.

537
01:05:26,816 --> 01:05:28,832
Phob, but your body...

538
01:05:29,904 --> 01:05:31,464
The villagers took me in and helped me.

539
01:05:33,168 --> 01:05:36,494
It took a long time for me to recover,

540
01:05:39,294 --> 01:05:40,542
and I never thought.

541
01:05:42,062 --> 01:05:43,408
I would see you again.

542
01:05:44,686 --> 01:05:46,328
- Phob…
- But in the end,

543
01:05:47,208 --> 01:05:48,448
I found my way back to you.

544
01:05:52,547 --> 01:05:54,368
Phob, please don't ever leave me again.

545
01:05:55,792 --> 01:05:59,179
Do you know how much
it hurt to be without you?

546
01:06:00,848 --> 01:06:01,849
No matter what happens,

547
01:06:03,040 --> 01:06:04,560
I will always find my way back to you,

548
01:06:06,696 --> 01:06:08,798
even if I must die a thousand deaths.

549
01:06:09,459 --> 01:06:10,859
Don't say another word about death.

550
01:06:13,168 --> 01:06:14,169
No more words.

551
01:06:16,715 --> 01:06:17,716
I won't let you say it.

552
01:06:27,070 --> 01:06:28,718
Your Phob is here.

553
01:06:33,054 --> 01:06:34,208
And I…

554
01:06:35,827 --> 01:06:37,718
will forever be yours,

555
01:06:39,086 --> 01:06:40,087
Your Highness.

556
01:06:41,902 --> 01:06:42,903
Love you.

557
01:06:45,728 --> 01:06:46,968
Love you, too.

558
01:08:01,288 --> 01:08:03,289
The End.

559
01:08:34,293 --> 01:08:35,294
Phob?

560
01:08:39,371 --> 01:08:40,372
You're still alive?

561
01:08:44,214 --> 01:08:45,215
Please give us a moment.

562
01:08:54,843 --> 01:08:58,268
It was all a misunderstanding.

563
01:08:59,926 --> 01:09:00,927
The body

564
01:09:01,888 --> 01:09:05,208
was so badly mutilated
that it couldn't be identified,

565
01:09:06,203 --> 01:09:08,448
and Phob's rings were found at the scene.

566
01:09:09,558 --> 01:09:11,675
That's why they mistakenly
believed it was him.

567
01:09:12,678 --> 01:09:14,064
You're one tough bastard to kill.

568
01:09:15,371 --> 01:09:16,491
Even Hell wouldn't take you.

569
01:09:22,472 --> 01:09:23,998
I have news to report.

570
01:09:24,766 --> 01:09:27,006
The government has ordered
a reduction in your sentence.

571
01:09:29,179 --> 01:09:30,288
You will not be executed,

572
01:09:31,595 --> 01:09:33,792
but sentenced to life imprisonment instead.

573
01:09:51,736 --> 01:09:52,737
And…

574
01:09:54,350 --> 01:09:56,702
I also wish to beg your forgiveness

575
01:10:19,947 --> 01:10:20,948
for what happened

576
01:10:22,710 --> 01:10:24,088
and for whatever reason.

577
01:10:26,256 --> 01:10:27,408
I may have caused

578
01:10:28,376 --> 01:10:30,648
the Varakulvatin Palace
to suffer such loss.

579
01:10:33,406 --> 01:10:34,407
You and I

580
01:10:35,598 --> 01:10:37,268
will never see eye to eye.

581
01:10:39,814 --> 01:10:40,848
Even today,

582
01:10:41,584 --> 01:10:44,048
I still don't believe your ideology,

583
01:10:44,235 --> 01:10:46,742
or what you stand for is right.

584
01:10:48,475 --> 01:10:51,048
Even if it costs me my life,
I will never believe otherwise.

585
01:10:55,598 --> 01:10:57,427
But there's one thing I believe in...

586
01:11:01,182 --> 01:11:03,648
your feelings for Tin

587
01:11:14,758 --> 01:11:15,768
are genuine.

588
01:11:28,068 --> 01:11:29,328
Listen to me, Phob.

589
01:11:30,960 --> 01:11:33,264
You owe the Varakulvatin
family a debt of gratitude.

590
01:11:34,166 --> 01:11:36,944
We raised you and supported
you until you came of age.

591
01:11:38,432 --> 01:11:39,433
About that debt,

592
01:11:40,245 --> 01:11:42,251
you'll never repay it in this lifetime.

593
01:11:46,011 --> 01:11:47,251
I am well aware, Your Highness.

594
01:11:49,680 --> 01:11:50,681
Therefore,

595
01:11:54,032 --> 01:11:56,736
you will take good care of my son.

596
01:12:12,438 --> 01:12:15,808
I swear it with my life, Your Highness.

597
01:12:52,974 --> 01:12:53,975
Hey.

598
01:12:54,622 --> 01:12:56,990
Make my brother cry again,

599
01:12:57,907 --> 01:12:59,027
and I'll break out of prison

600
01:12:59,496 --> 01:13:01,388
just to punch you in the face.

601
01:13:08,616 --> 01:13:10,928
I knew there had to be
something going on that night.

602
01:13:31,232 --> 01:13:33,008
Ugh, you two are disgustingly cute.

603
01:13:43,152 --> 01:13:45,494
Your Highness, let's have dinner.

604
01:14:00,472 --> 01:14:01,712
It's hard to believe, isn't it?

605
01:14:03,480 --> 01:14:06,376
We've been through so much together,

606
01:14:08,830 --> 01:14:11,390
and yet here we are today,
still given the chance to be together.

607
01:14:12,371 --> 01:14:14,048
Everything is bound to change.

608
01:14:15,462 --> 01:14:16,463
As the country changes,

609
01:14:17,824 --> 01:14:18,825
so do its people.

610
01:14:20,214 --> 01:14:22,603
The nation must move forward,

611
01:14:24,646 --> 01:14:25,647
and its people

612
01:14:26,331 --> 01:14:29,392
must learn to live together.

613
01:14:31,851 --> 01:14:32,852
You're right.

614
01:14:33,669 --> 01:14:35,888
Nothing ever stays the same.

615
01:14:36,670 --> 01:14:39,128
Someday, the country will change again,

616
01:14:40,443 --> 01:14:42,294
and the world will change with it.

617
01:14:43,168 --> 01:14:47,008
Who knows how far those changes will go?

618
01:14:50,771 --> 01:14:52,040
But there's one thing.

619
01:14:53,403 --> 01:14:54,528
I don't want to change.

620
01:14:56,923 --> 01:14:57,924
What is it?

621
01:15:00,163 --> 01:15:01,678
You and me.

622
01:15:04,142 --> 01:15:07,968
You once said that if
this world had freedom,

623
01:15:09,403 --> 01:15:11,547
our love would be easier.

624
01:15:13,584 --> 01:15:14,968
Do you still believe that?

625
01:15:15,931 --> 01:15:16,932
I do, Your Highness.

626
01:15:18,091 --> 01:15:21,568
Change can never be
achieved in a single generation.

627
01:15:24,387 --> 01:15:25,648
What we've done

628
01:15:26,398 --> 01:15:28,608
may be only a small step

629
01:15:29,555 --> 01:15:30,656
toward a happier life

630
01:15:31,507 --> 01:15:32,928
for those who come after us.

631
01:15:35,299 --> 01:15:36,408
One day,

632
01:15:37,182 --> 01:15:40,048
love will no longer be
hindered by social rank

633
01:15:40,712 --> 01:15:41,808
or differences,

634
01:15:44,163 --> 01:15:45,368
and two people

635
01:15:46,371 --> 01:15:48,749
will be able to love
each other without fear.

636
01:15:54,430 --> 01:15:56,937
I don't know when that day will come,

637
01:15:58,831 --> 01:16:02,248
but we're fortunate

638
01:16:03,336 --> 01:16:04,648
to have each other today.

639
01:16:07,299 --> 01:16:08,300
Phob,

640
01:16:09,482 --> 01:16:10,682
will you stay with me forever?

641
01:16:14,078 --> 01:16:15,079
Yes, I will.

642
01:16:53,171 --> 01:16:54,172
I'll put it on you.

643
01:17:08,642 --> 01:17:09,888
I promise you.

644
01:17:12,414 --> 01:17:14,928
I will be

645
01:17:15,480 --> 01:17:16,481
your prince

646
01:17:18,088 --> 01:17:19,089
forever.

647
01:17:25,208 --> 01:17:26,248
I love you, Your Highness.

648
01:17:27,603 --> 01:17:28,604
I love you, too.

649
01:18:12,035 --> 01:18:13,648
I want Ran Juan soup.

650
01:18:16,353 --> 01:18:17,808
Why don't you try this soup instead?

651
01:18:18,208 --> 01:18:21,808
This mixed veggies soup
is delicious. Aum made it.

652
01:18:24,694 --> 01:18:26,208
You two are spoiling him.

653
01:18:27,675 --> 01:18:29,968
You're the best, dear.

654
01:18:30,070 --> 01:18:32,088
May your wish come true, dear.

655
01:18:32,128 --> 01:18:34,648
- I love you the most.
- I love you, too.

656
01:18:34,788 --> 01:18:36,708
Come on, you should
put it on. I want to see it.

657
01:18:36,754 --> 01:18:37,412
Sure.

658
01:18:37,436 --> 01:18:39,434
This one is quite old. You
should stop wearing it already.

659
01:18:39,510 --> 01:18:41,565
I will put it on now.

660
01:18:41,619 --> 01:18:43,528
Here, let me help you with that.

661
01:18:45,902 --> 01:18:47,968
Wow, what a man.

662
01:19:36,974 --> 01:19:38,088
What is this?

663
01:19:38,368 --> 01:19:39,848
What is this?

664
01:19:41,992 --> 01:19:44,468
Thank you!
